# Example A — a single paper that rebuts and undercuts ITSELF
#
# Purpose: kill the intuition that "one paper cannot rebut itself." The unit of argumentation in
# LARA is the support term (spec §6), NOT the paper. One honest empirical paper contributes
# several support terms, several leaves, AND several attacks — its limitations section, its
# robustness appendix, and its ablations are attacks the same paper mounts on its own headline
# claim. All three attack kinds below originate inside `paper_17`.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle, per worked-examples-plan §0).

artifact paper_17 at sha256:aaaa...
policy empirical-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim ------------------------------------------------------------------------

claim c1
  nl      = "Method M improves accuracy on distribution D"
  formal  = improves(M, accuracy, D)
  binding = { author = alice, audit-status = reviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves (all from the SAME paper) -------------------------------------------------

leaf e1 : reports(exp_3, effect(M, accuracy, D, positive))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [evidence/table_2.csv#row=mean]

leaf e2 : randomized(exp_3)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = user
  refs       = [paper_17.pdf#sec=4.1]

leaf e3 : powered(exp_3)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = user
  refs       = [paper_17.pdf#sec=4.1]

# The paper's OWN limitations section reports an eval-distribution shift...
leaf e4 : distribution_shift(M, accuracy, D)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = user
  refs       = [paper_17.pdf#sec=7-limitations]

# ...and the paper's OWN robustness appendix reports the headline metric is an instrument
# artifact — the declared contrary of the leaf the main support relies on.
leaf e5 : instrument_artifact(M, accuracy, D)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [paper_17.pdf#appendix=C]

# The measurement leaf the support term's frontier rests on (undermine target).
leaf e6 : measured(M, accuracy, D, positive)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [evidence/table_2.csv#row=raw]

# --- The support argument for the headline claim -----------------------------------------------

arg a1 : supports(c1) by controlled_experiment(M, accuracy, D, exp_3)
  discharge randomization     with e2
  discharge adequate_power    with e3
  discharge external_validity with e6   # rests on the raw measurement leaf e6
# NOTE: external_validity is discharged (not left open) so this example exercises DEFEAT, not a
# gap. The planned E2 covers the open-hole/gap path; here we want live attacks.

# --- Three attacks, ALL from the same paper ----------------------------------------------------

# (1) UNDERCUT — the limitations section defeats external validity. Licensed by
# `exception controlled_experiment : distribution_shift(...)`. Undercuts ALWAYS succeed
# regardless of preference (spec §7): "the rule does not apply here."
arg d1 : challenges(external_validity(a1)) by leaf(e4)
undercut d1 a1.rule

# (2) UNDERMINE — the robustness appendix attacks the measurement LEAF e6 that discharges
# external_validity. `instrument_artifact` is a declared contrary of `measured(...,positive)`.
arg d2 : challenges(e6) by leaf(e5)
undermine d2 a1.external_validity.leaf

# (3) REBUT — a second in-paper experiment (a null ablation) concludes the contrary of the
# headline claim. Rebut targets the defeasible root conclusion of a1.
leaf e7 : reports(exp_9, effect(M, accuracy, D, negligible))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [evidence/table_5.csv#row=ablation]

arg d3 : supports(c1_neg) by null_result(M, accuracy, D, exp_9)
  discharge randomization  with e2
  discharge adequate_power with e3
rebut d3 a1

status c1

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Arguments in the compiled AF (all complete; a1 has its CQs discharged):
#   a1  -> out    (attacked by d1 undercut, d2 undermine, and d3 rebut; each is unattacked, so
#                  each is `in`, driving a1 to `out` under grounded semantics)
#   d1  -> in
#   d2  -> in
#   d3  -> in
# Claim status:
#   c1  -> defeated   (its only support a1 is `out`; spec §8 aggregation)
#
# Teaching point: every edge here has source and target inside paper_17. "A paper cannot rebut
# itself" is a category error — the paper is not a node. The self-attacks are exactly where the
# paper is honest about its own limits, and LARA turns that honesty into a computed `defeated`.
